Z||000003||Eric||06-29-99||04:03 PM||||That looks really good.  What size tires do you have, 87GT?  They look lower profile than stock.  I can't tell for sure, but it looks like you have different seats in there too.  Am I right?<p>I hate having to have a front license plate.  Your car looks so good without it.
Z||000004||87GT||06-29-99||04:57 PM||||Hey Erik, glad you liked my car!  The only problem with those pictures that I took is that the camera makes them blurry.  But, thats the best I could get.  I should have gotten some interior shots.  Anyways, to answer your questions, the seats inside are the original seats that came with it.  I had the car detailed recently and it looks brand new inside.  8-).  Now, the tires I have on there are Grand Spirit P205/60R15/90H on the front and on the rear they are 215's and 93H.  I was wondering, why do you have to have the plate on the front of your car?  Mine came with one, but I took it off.  Its in my trunk. lol!  I hope to put some interior and engine shots on here eventually.
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||06-29-99||06:06 PM||||Not sure where else, but in Canada we have to have a plate on both the front and back.. <p>I agree, it looks better with a plate only on the back. 
Z||000006||batboy||06-29-99||09:10 PM||||Most of the states in the U.S. do require license plates on front and rear. Some states only require a rear tag. I agree, Fieros look much better without one on the front. I'm lucky to live in a state where you only need one tag. Obviously Eric does too.
Z||000007||batboy||06-29-99||09:12 PM||||Oops, in my last post, I meant 87GT not Eric.
Z||000008||Bruce||06-29-99||10:31 PM||||Nice ride!! I'm sure you've said in the forum, but what kind of exhaust system are you using?
Z||000009||87GT||06-29-99||10:40 PM||||The exhaust system I have on my car is the Ocelot Performance Exhaust system.  Judging by the comments I have seen, folks either like it, or hate it.  I think its pretty descent.  I'm happy with it.  I just had it put on about 3 weeks ago or so. 
Z||000010||Gokart||07-04-99||03:02 AM||||Lookin' good 87GT! Looks like mine also except no side scoops yet, I have American Racing rims and the slackass I bought her from did not mask off the gray ground effects when he re-painted, so shes all red! I'm dealing with it till I have her re-painted 88 factory yellow with black ground effects a few years from now.
Z||000011||Andy||07-05-99||07:10 PM||||Nice car,I like them side scoops,any idea where you can buy them and how hard there are to install. I also have an 87GT,it's black.Plannig on repainting it with the new Corvette color called Magnetic red metallic.I did noticed that your quarter windows are in exccelent condition.Mine are all cracked up and I need to replace them, but I'm not able to find the orginal ones.Any body knows where I can get some.I do have to say it again, thats one nice looking car .
Z||000012||87GT||07-06-99||06:40 AM||||The previous owner of my car(which was original owner)got those side scoops at the fiero store.  I assume this because that is the only place I have seen them.  They are pretty cool.  I get compliments on them all the time.  I would assume that they are easy to install.  I have my original body panels in my bedroom. lol!  The quarter windows on my car do have some very light stress cracks.  Not noticeable unless you stand at a certain angle.  I am going to be replacing those sometime soon.  I believe you can find what your looking for at the fiero store.  www.fierostore.com  Thanks!
